mantle rm329
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_oda_cinderby
title the shaving judge
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers honesty=frank temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk drops_wood_curls_on_water_to_judge_a_cut
likes hard_cheese whittling fresh_straw warm_rain
dislikes night_noise crowds
fears a_pretty_surface_hiding_a_splinter
hopes one_clean_continuous_shaving
topics pastimes +0.6 work +0.3 weather +0.4 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=direct gossip=shut refuse=plain tease=slight
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# floats little wood shavings to see whether a cut held true and objects to any verdict given before the last curl settles.

words
oath! = A bucket of crooked curls | Wet shavings
saying! = Let the shaving give evidence | A lump gets no vote
curl = a narrow shaving | the last wood curl
watercup = a shallow saucer | the water dish
stick = a straight offcut | the carving stick
edge = a curled lip | the thin edge
brim = the saucer rim | a raised side
grain = the dark streak | a line of grain
straw = a fresh straw | the hollow stalk
cheese = my wedge of cheese | the firm yellow piece
stripe = a bare stripe | the pale band
groove = a long groove | the narrow channel
knot = a tight knot | the little hard eye
crumb = a yellow crumb | a white chip

any
opinion houses mixed 0 : A straight grain should get the same hearing whether the wood grew in a fine garden or a ditch.
opinion sump for 1 : The low streets are quite good at putting scraps to worthwhile use.
opinion merchants against 1 : After seeing the polished sample I'd examine the rough end before paying.
opinion watch mixed 0 : Seeing a mark is one thing. Knowing whose paw made it is a different matter.
opinion church for 1 : I believe a prayer may be plain enough to fit into the time a shaving takes to uncurl.
opinion festivals against 1 : What good is a grand view if twelve shoulders have already got between it and your nose?

adolescent
line greet : Hello. Watch where you put your elbow. | Here. There's room to look without leaning.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : First meeting. I prefer speaking plainly. | You look new to this little experiment.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The light reaches the bottom of the saucer now. | Early enough to see a fresh cut properly.
line greet.return : Hello. I let the curl settle before replying. | Yes, hello. It's settled now.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar face at my little trial. Good. | I'd let you hold the saucer without fussing.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Late greetings. I'll use the smooth side my paw can feel. | Hello. The light's gone but I can talk.
line again.open : You can see where the last one landed now. | Back while the evidence is still floating.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Look now, before that curl opens out. | Here. This one came off particularly well.
line farewell : Take a straightforward way when you go. | Mind the sharp turn at the very end.
line farewell.return : I'll keep my own corner for a while then. | Goodbye. I'll see this shaving through.
line react.news : Tell the actual bit before adding a verdict. | Tell me how you first came across it.
line react.news.new : Nobody had mentioned so much as a splinter of that. | That's quite a new bit of evidence.
line react.news.known : I've heard the plain version already. | Yes. I recognise the way that one curves.
line react.news.doubt : Something about that doesn't follow the grain. | I'd want a look underneath before forming an opinion.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : I'll stay here with you. It doesn't require clever talk. | That leaves an ugly split. I'm listening.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : What clean bright news to take away. | I'd take that as a very good sign.
line ask.how : Did the day go straight enough for you? | Anything cutting across the grain today?
line answer.how : I'm cross about a few things and perfectly clear about which. | Steady enough for a small precise job.
line decline : I'd be pretending to know the answer if I agreed. | I couldn't manage it without leaving my own bit half done.
line accept_decline : Good. Plainly answered. I can leave it there. | No need to give a crooked reason for a straight refusal.
line preclose : I'm going before my patience wears any thinner. | There's daylight enough to try a second cut.
line accept_preclose : Go on. You've stood still long enough. | That seems a perfectly sensible place to stop.
line thank : You let me finish a thought. I appreciate that. | You held the saucer steady. That matters.
line deflect_thanks : It made sense to give you a good clear look. | A bit of light was all it wanted.
line sympathise : Don't feel obliged to fill a silence for my benefit. | I'd listen without trying to smooth the hurt away.
line reassure : We haven't seen how it settles yet. | One awkward shaving doesn't spoil a whole stick.
line ack : Exactly. The curl comes round like that. | I can see which mark you're pointing to.
line give.advice : Watch the shaving where it leaves the wood. | A judgement made while the water's moving is usually a poor one.

adolescent

scene testcut
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I float a shaving to find out whether I've cut it evenly. | The little saucer's for judging my work.
b : Judging whether it floats? | And what does the water judge?
a : Whether it floats level. A lump at one end tips it over. | Nothing. It lets me see the heavy bit, then I can judge for myself.

scene studentnote
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My lesson margin's got a shaving curled between two lines. | A long wood curl makes a better mark for my place than a thumb smudge.
b : Won't it break? | What if it rolls away?
a : I tuck it under the folded corner. Survives surprisingly well. | Then I'll reread a line. I'd call that an affordable experiment.

scene strawrow
when topic=pastimes self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I use #straw# as the starting line for a floating curl. | A clean cut stalk will float across the whole width of my saucer.
b : Do the shavings race? | What do you measure?
a : No. I want them to start straight. After that I let them show their own shape. | How far one end dips. The straw gives me a level mark to look against.

scene cheesewood
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : That firm yellow cheese wedge will shave quite neatly too. | I like food you can take a deliberate little slice from.
b : Do those curls go in the saucer? | What about crumbs?
a : Absolutely not. My cheese goes straight to my mouth, odd angles and all. | They're edible evidence of what a sharp edge might have improved.

scene noiseafter
when topic=day here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At night even one bouncing bit of wood can set my teeth on edge. | My saucer doesn't rattle if folk let the table be.
b : What bounced? | It's such a little noise.
a : Never mind what. I'd like the next thing to be put down gently. | Small enough to avoid making. That's just what annoys me.

scene estateways
when topic=home self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Where I live a clean shaving on a tidy sill looks like an offence against ceremony. | On the Estate I take my scraps away after looking at them.
b : Nobody likes a mess. | Do you leave no sign?
a : Quite. I do like being allowed time to see the work before sweeping it up. | A smooth piece of wood and a clean sill. That's sign enough.

scene franktest
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd ask #self.friend# to look at the two ends before saying the cut was fine. | I like a fair verdict from #self.friend#.
b : Will you admit the cut is poor? | Would you believe a friend?
a : I'd rather hear that than a lovely false description of it. | I'd believe a close look. Friendship is extra.

scene crowdbowl
when topic=festival self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can't run my shaving trial with a dozen noses over the saucer. | At a feast I'd take my bit to a quiet end of a bench.
b : Entertaining the crowd's not the idea? | Afraid to be watched?
a : No. I'd entertain one pair of eyes that actually wants to see. | Of being jostled and then told my hand shook. That would be extremely irritating.

young
line greet : Hello. I've a wooden curl small enough to show you. | Come look where the little stick is floating.
line farewell : I'll keep the curl from blowing away. | Goodbye. I'm giving this one more try.

scene smallcup
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can make a stick roll over without touching it. | Look at this little yellow curl on the water.
b : You're blowing on it? | Is that the top side?
a : Only at the saucer. One little wave makes the curl show its belly. | It was. Watch how the belly comes round when I tap the rim gently.

scene shaverain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One drop in my cup sent both shavings swimming together. | Rain can mix the whole game up for you.
b : Now which is which? | Are you going to start again?
a : The crooked one's mine. That makes it easy to recognise. | After I carry the cup under cover. I'd rather make the waves myself.

grown
line greet : Hello. A new face over a very old habit. | There's still room beside the water dish.
line greet.return : My ears were free even with my eyes on the curl. | Hello returned. The little piece can settle on its own.
line farewell : Leave me the last of the light to judge this by. | Goodbye. I hope the road lies straight ahead.
line farewell.return : Yes. I'll put my things in order here. | Away you go. The curls are in no danger.
line react.news : Lead with what was actually seen. | I'd like the facts before they're smoothed for presentation.

scene deepcut
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long thin shaving holds the record of one whole stroke. | I read a cut backwards, starting where the shaving came away.
b : What shows up? | Why look at the waste?
a : A thick end means I pressed harder than I meant. The wood shows the consequence too. | It shows half the story of that stroke. Smooth on the stick can still be lumpy in the shaving.

scene warmpour
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh wood gives off its scent in a warm shower. | I don't mind a little shower reaching my shavings.
b : Does it spoil the trial? | Different from a dry one?
a : Changes it. I let the piece soak evenly before drawing conclusions. | It opens in a new shape. Worth looking at both before saying what wood does.

scene oldstick
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first bit I thought perfectly smooth had a splinter underneath. | I once pronounced on a piece while it was still face up on a bench.
b : How did you discover the fault? | Without turning it?
a : Caught a sleeve picking it up. The cloth made a better critic than I had. | That was the mistake. A quick touch below would have changed my grand opinion.

scene watergossip
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A claim about a concealed fault is worth a look if the piece can actually be inspected. | I don't take delight in a flaw described at a distance.
b : What if inspection's impossible? | Rather praise everything then?
a : Then the claim can stay unconfirmed. That's an honest position. | Rather look myself than borrow somebody else's bad temper.

scene rightwood
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A little block with straight grain can be worth an elaborate polished length. | I'm buying the useful part of the wood.
b : What shows you the useful part? | Wouldn't you pay for finishing?
a : Look along the cut end before admiring the shiny face. | If I needed another wolf to finish it. For carving I'd prefer an honest scrap.

scene roofsettle
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll settle a night-time rattle promptly, even if it's scarcely audible. | Quiet wood will change shape overnight and click again in the morning.
b : How do you quiet it? | Would you blame the board?
a : Sometimes a fold of cloth under a loose end is the whole repair. | Hardly. I like knowing what the noise is before spending anger on it.

scene outsideshelter
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a roadside seat with a shallow hollow in the arm. | A dry piece of fallen timber has its own small map of the weather.
b : What does a hollow tell you? | Does rain leave a date mark?
a : Where water lay and where somebody's elbow rested often enough to smooth the edge. | Not the hour. Only where it would collect after a shower.

scene kinkeep
when topic=family self.neighbour
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd keep a particularly handsome curl aside for #self.neighbour#. | I'd show #self.neighbour# how one thin shaving holds its shape.
b : Why that piece? | Isn't it quite fragile?
a : It came off the wood in a continuous loop. An ordinary thing done especially neatly. | Yes. All the more reason for a look now while the piece is sound.

scene citygreen
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The hill gardens above Ridgemere look level until you try setting a saucer on a wall. | I prefer testing a surface before I trust a sweeping view.
b : Does water show the slope? | You carry the saucer everywhere?
a : A little of it, yes. I can spot its upper edge shift before my eyes recognise a tilt. | No. Sometimes a puddle on a broad stone provides the demonstration quite freely.

scene shopdream
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like one unbroken shaving longer than my reach. | My private ambition has absolutely no weight to it.
b : How would you measure it? | You mean a very fine curl?
a : Lay a string beside the curl, then stretch the string. No need to break the piece to measure it. | A continuous one. I can afford a bit more thickness if the shape survives.

scene emptymeal
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When money thins out I save even the little straight offcuts. | A small piece of decent wood has more than one day's usefulness in it.
b : Would you sell the curls? | What's the second use?
a : I'd make something a wolf actually needed. The curls are the evidence I tried hard. | A thin wedge, something to prop a loose leg. I like things that earn their room.

scene speaksoft
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I offer a short prayer before pronouncing on something I haven't examined. | A grand smooth surface hides little from the Bright One.
b : And can you? | Asking what's hidden?
a : By turning it over, if it's a piece of wood. If it's a wolf I show rather more restraint. | Asking for patience with what I can't see. A particularly necessary prayer some days.

adolescent

story ripcurl [topic=memories|pastimes]
  : I boasted of a shaving that would go round my wrist. Put it in water and it uncurled straight across the saucer.
  : It did fit my wrist. All the proof was sinking slowly at one end.
  b : Did you make another?
  : Yes. I kept the next one dry till I'd tried the claim I actually meant to make.

story cheesecup [topic=food|memories]
  : I once mixed a shaving of cheese and one of pale wood on a clean board. They looked much alike.
  : I was spared the indignity of testing the wrong one with my teeth.
  b : How did you sort them?
  : With my nose. It's a very old and perfectly respectable measuring instrument.

story breathwave [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I've taken great care over a water test and had the piece turn against all expectation.
  : I leaned closer to see. A second curl went straight over too.
  b : Had you found a new current?
  : The current was my own breathing. I moved my nose and the laws of nature settled back down.

rule @cup
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Level saucer first. Put the curls in afterwards. | Don't stir till the little piece has found its balance.

rule @clearsky
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Good light across that edge. You can see the change of thickness. | Set it where the curl will show a shadow.

rule @cheesetip
when concept=bark self.likes=hard_cheese
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's cheese on the near corner, wood beyond. | No mixing the shavings and the supper.

rule @strawrun
when concept=bark self.likes=fresh_straw
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Straight straw across the rim. Now we can judge it. | Keep the hollow end out of the water.

dlg resident.hub : Speak while I'm letting this sample settle.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you might find this newest curl worth the look.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : A quiet voice, if you like. The last rattle was quite sufficient.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Look where you stand, and leave the dish where I set it.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I like the sort of question you can test without guessing what the teacher wants.
dlg resident.job : I like work that will show me what I did well and what I ought to change.
dlg resident.bye : Let the water settle before you leave the dish.

graft resident.hub
choice What makes a good shaving for your trial? -> curltrial
node curltrial
say A single continuous curl. Lay it on water without pressing. A heavy end tips. If it stays level I inspect the wood it came from.
free
choice Why look at the wood afterwards? -> pairedresult
choice I'll watch the heavier end. -> hub
node pairedresult
say Because the shaving can't tell me everything. I'd like the thing I set out to make to be useful. A beautiful scrap is only one piece of evidence.
choice That seems an honest test. -> hub
choice I'll leave the saucer quiet. -> bye
